    item("DHARMa residual",
         "DHARMa simulates new possible outcomes from the fitted model (\\(n_\\text{sim}=250\\) by default), conditional on each ",
         "observation's fitted value. A DHARMa residual is then the proportion of simulated values that are lower than the actual ",
         "observation. If the model is well-specified, the DHARMa residuals are approximately uniformly distributed, between 0 and 1, ",
         "due to the universality of the uniform."),
    item("Universality of the uniform",
         "If you know the cumulative distribution function \\(F(.)\\) of the distribution that a sample \\(y\\) comes from, ",
